WEBVTT

00:00.640 --> 00:03.220
<i>After managing to get Morisaki back on his feet,</i>

00:03.220 --> 00:07.900
<i>Tsubasa and Misaki began their skillful attack on Meiwa FC.</i>

00:07.900 --> 00:12.570
<i>Not to be outdone, Kojiro stole the ball from Misaki with a powerful tackle.</i>

00:12.570 --> 00:14.880
<i>Using his fierce, rough play,</i>

00:14.880 --> 00:17.360
<i>he blows past everyone in his way and scores with a volley.</i>

00:17.360 --> 00:21.990
<i>The match gradually becomes a competition between their styles.</i>

00:21.990 --> 00:26.500
<i>Unrelenting, the two aces take the match to a draw until the final moment.</i>

00:26.500 --> 00:29.920
<i>The stadium is loud and roaring with applause for the two of them!</i>

00:29.920 --> 00:33.090
<i>This match, which started with a showdown between Tsubasa and Hyuga,</i>

00:33.090 --> 00:35.590
<i>constantly featured exchanges between them.</i>

00:37.220 --> 00:39.720
<i>Tsubasa slips on the mud and loses his footing!</i>

00:39.720 --> 00:40.970
Chance!

00:41.060 --> 00:41.680
Now!

00:41.680 --> 00:45.230
<i>Hyuga can't shoot! Tsubasa kicks it away!</i>

00:45.230 --> 00:48.020
This guy faked his slip to trap me!

00:48.020 --> 00:49.060
<i>The final whistle —</i>

00:56.820 --> 01:00.070
<i>It... It's a goal!</i>

01:00.070 --> 01:02.700
<i>Nankatsu loses the match!</i>

01:05.720 --> 01:07.290
<i>Damn it...!</i>

01:07.290 --> 01:10.250
<i>This guy... is crying?</i>

01:12.590 --> 01:14.670
You're Kojiro Hyuga, right?

01:15.560 --> 01:18.120
I'm here to scout you.

01:32.010 --> 01:37.640
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

01:32.010 --> 01:37.640
<i>koronda toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

01:37.640 --> 01:42.640
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

01:37.640 --> 01:42.640
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

01:43.310 --> 01:48.480
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

01:43.310 --> 01:48.480
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

01:49.190 --> 01:56.840
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

01:49.190 --> 01:56.840
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

01:56.840 --> 02:02.580
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

01:56.840 --> 02:02.580
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

02:02.580 --> 02:11.090
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

02:02.580 --> 02:11.090
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

02:11.090 --> 02:16.890
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

02:11.090 --> 02:16.890
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

02:16.890 --> 02:22.810
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

02:16.890 --> 02:22.810
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

02:22.810 --> 02:24.310
<i>Run & Run!</i>

02:24.310 --> 02:31.610
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

02:24.310 --> 02:31.610
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

02:31.610 --> 02:34.530
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Let's go, it's kickoff!</i>

02:31.610 --> 02:34.530
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kickoff</i>

02:34.530 --> 02:39.450
<i>Leap out into a giant field of dreams</i>

02:34.530 --> 02:39.450
<i>tobidasô dodekai dream field</i>

02:50.310 --> 02:54.270
<b><b>EPISODE 16:
THIS IS ACROBATIC FOOTBALL!</b></b>

02:52.060 --> 02:54.270
Me? At Toho Academy?

02:54.270 --> 02:57.090
As you might know, Toho Academy

02:57.090 --> 03:00.780
is a famous school that focuses on developing professional football players.

03:00.780 --> 03:04.370
We are quite ready to invite you on board.

03:04.370 --> 03:07.950
Besides your football skills, Hyuga, we've also looked into

03:07.950 --> 03:12.540
your personality and your daily life environment.

03:12.540 --> 03:15.560
If you were to join our academy,

03:15.560 --> 03:17.360
during Junior High, High School

03:17.360 --> 03:20.130
and College —about 10 years—

03:20.130 --> 03:22.210
then we'd cover all of your daily and academic expenses.

03:22.210 --> 03:23.970
All of it would be taken care by us.

03:23.970 --> 03:25.220
Are you for real?

03:25.220 --> 03:26.840
Of course.

03:26.840 --> 03:28.430
If you were to come to our academy,

03:28.430 --> 03:31.310
you could be able focus on the football you love so much.

03:32.940 --> 03:35.480
But, there are some conditions.

03:35.480 --> 03:36.760
Conditions?

03:36.760 --> 03:37.900
Conditions.

03:37.900 --> 03:39.550
You're not the only one we've kept our eyes on.

03:39.550 --> 03:42.120
We've been eyeing Tsubasa Ozora as a potential forward,

03:42.120 --> 03:45.200
even before the tournament started.

03:45.200 --> 03:49.890
We decided we'd scout whoever won the previous match.

03:49.890 --> 03:52.580
Meiwa, of course, was the winner.

03:52.580 --> 03:58.270
But we think deciding whether you or Tsubasa was the better player

03:58.270 --> 04:00.690
based on that match alone might've been a little too difficult.

04:00.690 --> 04:01.940
What are you saying?

04:01.940 --> 04:03.720
There's no way I'd lose to him!

04:03.720 --> 04:05.580
It should be be obvious I'm the best of the two!

04:05.580 --> 04:07.300
We won the match, and that's the truth!

04:07.300 --> 04:09.390
So: I am asking you to win the tournament.

04:09.390 --> 04:10.310
Eh!

04:10.310 --> 04:13.600
If you are as good as you say you are,

04:13.600 --> 04:15.860
prove it by winning the tournament.

04:15.860 --> 04:18.880
If you can manage to do that,

04:18.880 --> 04:22.280
then we, then Toho Academy, will offer you a football scholarship.

04:22.280 --> 04:23.990
You're serious?

04:23.990 --> 04:25.910
Yes. I wouldn't lie.

04:25.910 --> 04:28.620
Then I'll win this tournament!

04:35.270 --> 04:37.760
You know, if you come in second place in the group stage,

04:37.760 --> 04:40.130
you still advance into the finals stage.

04:40.840 --> 04:44.980
It's possible you and Tsubasa will face each other again.

04:50.760 --> 04:54.050
<i>Meanwhile, Nankatsu SC, with Tsubasa as its captain,</i>

04:54.050 --> 04:56.440
<i>shrugs off the shock of losing to Meiwa FC</i>

04:56.440 --> 05:01.640
<i>and crushes Fukuoka's Osu SS with a score of 9-0,</i>

05:01.640 --> 05:04.690
<i>giving them their first win of the group stages.</i>

05:01.640 --> 05:02.950
Yes, yes!

05:02.950 --> 05:04.690
We won! We won!

05:04.690 --> 05:07.160
Now we're 1 and 1.

05:07.160 --> 05:08.950
Let's keep this up,

05:08.950 --> 05:10.950
and advance out of the group stages!

05:10.950 --> 05:13.740
Now, that's just too naive!

05:13.740 --> 05:15.540
The heck...?

05:15.540 --> 05:17.430
The winners of Group 1

05:17.430 --> 05:20.000
are gonna be Meiwa and us, Hanawa!

05:20.000 --> 05:23.660
Hanawa Youth Football Association, from Akita, right?

05:23.660 --> 05:26.030
We played at noon against Osu,

05:26.030 --> 05:30.390
that team you just beat —and we beat them 10-0!

05:30.390 --> 05:32.510
They scored one more goal than us.

05:32.510 --> 05:34.430
That's how it is!

05:34.430 --> 05:37.180
Aren't they the guys that from the train platform?

05:38.310 --> 05:39.460
<i>Masao!</i>

05:39.460 --> 05:40.750
<i>Nice pass!</i>

05:40.750 --> 05:46.860
<i>Yeah, those two were perfectly in sync with each other. They made a great combo!</i>

05:46.860 --> 05:50.820
We're about to play! You'd better watch our match closely!

05:50.820 --> 05:52.240
Argh...

05:55.040 --> 05:59.460
<i>Hanawa Youth Football Association versus Shimabara FC of Group 1!</i>

05:59.460 --> 06:01.540
<i>Hanawa's kick-off will start the game.</i>

06:02.670 --> 06:04.450
All right! Let's go, Masao!

06:04.450 --> 06:05.420
Okay, Kazuo!

06:13.680 --> 06:15.220
We did it!

06:15.220 --> 06:16.470
Yeah!

06:18.770 --> 06:21.650
SIGN: HANAWA FC 7 - 0 SHIMABARA FC

06:23.190 --> 06:25.440
Hanawa totally dominated that game.

06:25.440 --> 06:26.870
That was awesome.

06:26.870 --> 06:30.070
You know, now I'm really looking forward to our match with Hanawa.

06:30.070 --> 06:32.740
Yeah, I'm looking forward to it too.

06:32.740 --> 06:33.450
Win it!

06:33.450 --> 06:36.700
You bet I will. Brazil is waiting for me after all!

06:38.360 --> 06:43.240
<i>The next day, Nankatsu won their matches before and after noon without any difficulties,</i>

06:43.240 --> 06:47.210
<i>and their record is now three wins, one loss.</i>

06:47.210 --> 06:48.520
Yes, we did it!

06:48.520 --> 06:49.470
That's three, now!

06:49.470 --> 06:57.220
<i>Now, preparations have begun for tomorrow's match with Hanawa, with advancement from the Group stages at stake.</i>

06:57.220 --> 07:05.900
<i>However, that afternoon, Meiwa vs. Hanawa, the two undefeated teams of the group, clashed. And the result...</i>

07:08.070 --> 07:08.730
Yes!

07:08.730 --> 07:09.820
We did it!

07:09.820 --> 07:13.410
SIGN: MEIWA FC 5 - 5 HANAWA FC

07:10.600 --> 07:12.160
They drew with Meiwa?

07:12.160 --> 07:15.370
Now, if we don't win our game with Hanawa tomorrow and get a draw instead,

07:15.370 --> 07:18.370
we won't be able to advance to the finals...

07:23.370 --> 07:27.420
We'll finally be playing against Hanawa Youth Football Association tomorrow.

07:27.420 --> 07:31.260
If we don't win this match, we won't make it into the finals stage.

07:31.260 --> 07:36.200
So, in order to prepare for tomorrow, I'll now review Hanawa's strong points.

07:36.200 --> 07:40.100
Guys, please remember Hanawa's match with Shimabara FC.

07:41.030 --> 07:46.730
The specialty of this team relies on the perfect combination of their forwards, the Tachibana Twins.

07:46.730 --> 07:53.650
When they attack, they leave the offense to these two, while the team packs the midfield and concentrates on defending.

07:53.700 --> 07:56.530
Those two alone set the flow of the game.

07:56.530 --> 07:59.080
You're right. Shimabara couldn't do anything against them either.

07:59.080 --> 08:03.490
The key to Nankatsu's victory is to figure out

08:03.490 --> 08:05.640
how we can destroy those two's perfect teamwork.

08:05.640 --> 08:07.210
I have a plan just for that.

08:07.210 --> 08:08.040
Tsubasa.

08:08.040 --> 08:08.880
Yes!

08:08.880 --> 08:09.710
Misaki.

08:09.710 --> 08:10.590
Yes!

08:10.590 --> 08:13.220
I'm giving you two a mission!

08:18.860 --> 08:21.220
We have a heavy responsibility.

08:21.220 --> 08:22.300
Yes.

08:22.300 --> 08:26.440
But, I think that's a good way to counter that combination.

08:26.440 --> 08:29.040
I'll be counting on you tomorrow, Misaki.

08:29.040 --> 08:32.540
Likewise! I won't let Hanawa score even one go—

08:35.180 --> 08:36.420
Were you surprised?

08:36.420 --> 08:38.660
You should join us too!

08:40.960 --> 08:42.080
A pillow fight!

08:42.080 --> 08:42.910
All right!

08:42.910 --> 08:44.290
Let's do this!

08:46.500 --> 08:47.810
That hurt!

08:47.810 --> 08:50.420
Nishio, I'm sorry!

08:50.420 --> 08:51.440
Goal!

08:51.440 --> 08:53.260
You really are a striker, Tsubasa.

08:53.260 --> 08:56.260
Oh, shut up! Take this!

08:57.240 --> 08:58.730
How about this, Nishio!

08:58.730 --> 09:00.430
I'm an iron wall!

09:00.430 --> 09:03.270
Would you dare say that in front of Wakabayashi?

09:03.270 --> 09:05.430
Eat this shot!

09:06.760 --> 09:08.230
All right!

09:08.230 --> 09:09.020
Take this!

09:09.020 --> 09:10.690
Nice shot!

09:10.690 --> 09:17.560
they all say silly kid things on top of each other here

09:17.560 --> 09:20.570
Guys, let's use this power to beat Hanawa!

09:20.570 --> 09:22.240
Yeah!

09:28.820 --> 09:30.770
At the end of the second day of the tournament,

09:30.770 --> 09:33.870
we were able to see all the promising players, right?

09:33.870 --> 09:39.110
All save for Nankatsu SC's goalkeeper Genzo Wakabayashi, who didn't participate.

09:39.110 --> 09:40.220
Right.

09:40.220 --> 09:42.600
He's a genius who, despite being a 5th grader, lead Shutetsu Elementary

09:42.600 --> 09:46.740
and made them champions without conceding a single goal last year.

09:46.740 --> 09:49.310
No one comes close to him in this generation.

09:49.310 --> 09:52.200
What about Naniwa FC's Taichi Nakanishi?

09:52.200 --> 09:53.660
Well, he's a good goalkeeper.

09:53.660 --> 09:56.710
Despite having a large build, he's surprisingly agile.

09:56.710 --> 10:00.470
It's a shame, though, but there's just no comparing him to Wakabayashi, who's grown so much.

10:00.470 --> 10:02.370
What do you think of the midfielders?

10:02.370 --> 10:06.390
The ones who have left an impression on me are Nankatsu's Taro Misaki,

10:06.390 --> 10:11.460
Furano's Hikaru Matsuyama, and Meiwa FC's Takeshi Sawada.

10:11.460 --> 10:14.810
I'll consider the 4th grader Takeshi in two years,

10:14.810 --> 10:17.880
but Misaki and Matsuyama are players that I want.

10:17.880 --> 10:19.880
Hikaru Matsuyama...

10:19.880 --> 10:21.990
Don't you think that he lacks technique?

10:22.510 --> 10:28.500
He has huge potential and willpower. I value the fact he's the captain of a public elementary school football team

10:28.500 --> 10:30.390
that he led all the way to the National Tournament much more than his technique.

10:30.390 --> 10:34.250
We can always work on his technique after he joins.

10:35.170 --> 10:41.450
That said, Musashi FC's Jun Misugi stands out the most of all the midfielders.

10:41.450 --> 10:46.300
On top of having the qualities of a great playmaker, he is also a skilled scorer.

10:46.300 --> 10:49.560
Coach Kitazume of the Secondary School section did mention

10:49.560 --> 10:52.710
he wanted us to evaluate their ability to score.

10:52.710 --> 11:00.880
The prizes are without a doubt these two: Nankatsu SC's Tsubasa Ozora and Meiwa FC's Kojiro Hyuga.

11:00.880 --> 11:04.340
Even though we'd been eyeing Tsubasa since the prefectural tournament,

11:04.340 --> 11:07.860
he's shined brightly enough that, in two days, he's atop our National list.

11:07.860 --> 11:11.800
If he didn't do as much, he wouldn't be worth trying to get for our academy.

11:11.800 --> 11:16.790
I really want to see them play each other once again.

11:16.790 --> 11:19.780
Me too. In the finals.

11:22.040 --> 11:25.320
<i>It's the third day of the tournament and it's time for the last match of the group stage.</i>

11:25.910 --> 11:32.960
<i>Furano has put everything they've got in their play, and have advanced to the finals stage after winning all 5 matches.</i>

11:32.960 --> 11:38.010
<i>Musashi FC have also made their way through the group stage, winning all 5 of their matches</i>

11:38.010 --> 11:41.220
<i>while having the luxury of letting their captain Misugi resting on the bench. </i>

11:41.220 --> 11:45.880
<i>Meiwa also showed their overpowering strength in their last game,</i>

11:45.880 --> 11:47.970
<i>close the group stage by winning 4 out of 5 matches, with a lone draw.</i>

11:47.970 --> 11:53.770
<i>All of Nankatsu's rivals have advanced to the finals stage.</i>

11:53.770 --> 12:02.860
<i>The last game of the group stage, with the chance to advance out of the group on the line... Nankatsu vs. Hanawa is about to start.</i>

12:02.860 --> 12:09.030
<i>On one side, we have Nankatsu who gave us a historical match</i>

12:09.030 --> 12:13.080
<i>against the powerhouse Meiwa FC, with victory slipping away at the very end.</i>

12:13.080 --> 12:15.750
<i>On the other side, we have Hanawa, a team who fought on equal terms with Meiwa.</i>

12:15.750 --> 12:19.380
<i>The stadium is already packed to the brim with spectators, eager to watch this match.</i>

12:19.380 --> 12:20.980
Listen to me, boys!

12:20.980 --> 12:24.880
Today's match is an important one. We have a ticket to the finals at stake.

12:27.720 --> 12:28.600
We'll do whatever it takes. Win, and make it through the group stage!

12:28.600 --> 12:32.060
Good! Stick to the plan, Misaki, Tsubasa!

12:32.060 --> 12:33.140
Yes!

12:35.140 --> 12:37.960
<i>Both teams' players enter the field.</i>

12:37.960 --> 12:40.110
I trust you, guys.

12:40.110 --> 12:43.690
<i>The representatives of Akita Prefecture, Hanawa, have 3 wins and 1 draw so far.</i>

12:43.690 --> 12:46.810
<i>The Tachibana Twins are in charge of the offense, while the rest of the team focuses on defense.</i>

12:46.810 --> 12:50.150
<i>This is a rather unique team with a particular divide.</i>

12:50.150 --> 12:54.200
<i>On the other side, representing Shizuoka Prefecture, Nankatsu has 3 wins and 1 loss so far.</i>

12:54.200 --> 13:00.210
<i>With their ace striker Tsubasa at the center, this one's a superb team with great teamwork.</i>

13:00.210 --> 13:05.260
<i>Both teams' supporters passionately cry out before the start of the match.</i>

13:05.260 --> 13:10.000
<i>Amidst the loud cheering, the match is about to begin with Hanawa's kick-off.</i>

13:11.320 --> 13:15.810
<i>Who will advance to the finals stage in the end, Nankatsu or Hanawa?</i>

13:15.810 --> 13:17.760
All right, we'll score today too!

13:17.760 --> 13:18.150
Yeah!

13:18.150 --> 13:21.900
<i>Hanawa, as usual, gets to work on opening the score early with the Tachibana Twins' attack.</i>

13:21.900 --> 13:26.150
Guys, it's just them attacking! Do whatever you can and stop them!

13:26.150 --> 13:27.120
Let's go!

13:27.120 --> 13:30.660
<i>Can Nankatsu stop them here?</i>

13:37.420 --> 13:38.330
What?

13:38.760 --> 13:39.730
<i>It's useless!</i>

13:39.730 --> 13:43.840
<i>Even the famous Nankatsu is having trouble stopping them from breaking through the midfield.</i>

13:43.840 --> 13:46.840
Why? Why can they get past us so easily?

13:46.840 --> 13:50.850
<i>Masao and Kazuo Tachibana are in perfect harmony today.</i>

13:50.850 --> 13:53.430
<i>Will they be able to score a goal right after the start of this match?</i>

13:53.430 --> 13:54.640
Like I'd let you!

13:54.640 --> 13:55.460
Hey!

13:55.460 --> 13:56.520
Nice pass!

13:59.020 --> 14:00.810
We'll be your opponents!

14:00.810 --> 14:02.200
What?!

14:10.030 --> 14:12.030
Tachibana Twins eyecatch

14:10.030 --> 14:13.070
<i>What is this? Tsubasa was announced a center forward today,</i>

14:13.070 --> 14:14.450
<i>but he's far back on the field!</i>

14:14.450 --> 14:17.080
<i>He and Misaki are marking the Tachibana Twins!</i>

14:17.080 --> 14:19.500
<i>This looks like it's going to be a fun showdown.</i>

14:19.500 --> 14:21.780
Masao, these two can do it.

14:21.780 --> 14:22.250
Yeah.

14:22.250 --> 14:26.590
<i>What's this? The Tachibana Twins have paused their approach!</i>

14:26.590 --> 14:29.380
What are two you up to? If you won't come to us, then I'll just go to you!

14:29.380 --> 14:30.130
<i>Here's my chance!</i>

14:31.450 --> 14:32.050
Kazuo!

14:32.480 --> 14:33.400
Damn it!

14:33.400 --> 14:34.720
Nice, Misaki!

14:34.720 --> 14:37.420
<i>The ball is stolen away from the Tachibana Twins!</i>

14:37.420 --> 14:38.560
Did Masao and Kazuo just...?

14:38.560 --> 14:40.020
Go!

14:40.020 --> 14:42.480
<i>Tsubasa fires off a long pass.</i>

14:42.480 --> 14:43.670
Nice pass!

14:43.670 --> 14:45.670
<i>The ball goes to the midfielder, Izawa.</i>

14:45.670 --> 14:47.180
All right, let's go!

14:47.180 --> 14:48.170
Yes!

14:48.170 --> 14:51.950
<i>It's Nankatsu's famous Shutetsu Trio's turn to attack!</i>

14:51.950 --> 14:54.660
You know, I'm from Shutetsu, too...

14:54.660 --> 14:57.200
<i>However Hanawa's defense is quite thick.</i>

14:57.200 --> 15:00.410
<i>Will Nankatsu be able to break through and score?</i>

15:00.410 --> 15:02.410
Nankatsu is really strong.

15:02.410 --> 15:03.630
Don't let your guard down!

15:03.630 --> 15:04.700
Take this, Kisugi!

15:04.700 --> 15:05.750
Hey, Taki!

15:05.750 --> 15:07.130
Good!

15:07.130 --> 15:10.020
Hey, Tsubasa's going to shoot!

15:10.020 --> 15:11.220
Go after him, Kazuo!

15:13.140 --> 15:15.890
Nankatsu, just a little bit more!

15:15.890 --> 15:17.560
Hold on, Hanawa!

15:17.560 --> 15:20.080
<i>As expected, Hanawa's defense is tough!</i>

15:20.080 --> 15:23.940
<i>All the courses are covered and Nankatsu can't quite shoot!</i>

15:23.940 --> 15:25.610
All right, mark them thoroughly!

15:25.610 --> 15:27.360
Damn it!

15:30.240 --> 15:35.000
<i>Oh! Tsubasa, who was far back just a moment ago, rushes towards the goal!</i>

15:36.620 --> 15:37.580
Don't let him shoot!

15:37.580 --> 15:38.370
Yeah!

15:38.370 --> 15:39.950
Go!

15:40.640 --> 15:42.370
<i>It's no use! They can't keep up with him!</i>

15:42.370 --> 15:44.370
<i>Tsubasa lets off a mighty shot!</i>

15:46.270 --> 15:47.670
<i>It's in!</i>

15:47.670 --> 15:49.510
I did it!

15:50.920 --> 15:52.260
That was awesome, Tsubasa!

15:52.260 --> 15:53.720
We did it!

15:52.620 --> 15:56.290
<i>Tsubasa fired directly at the goal with no hesitation!</i>

15:56.290 --> 16:01.640
<i>The defense that Hanawa so often boasted about couldn't do anything against Tsubasa's bullet shot!</i>

16:01.640 --> 16:03.940
<i>The little football kid finally gets a chance to show his skills!</i>

16:03.940 --> 16:08.830
<i>With this, Tsubasa surpasses Hyuga's 17 goals</i>

16:08.830 --> 16:11.860
<i>and is now in the lead as top scorer of the tournament!</i>

16:11.860 --> 16:14.780
Masao! That guy is really amazing!

16:14.780 --> 16:17.450
You're right. But we're just getting started.

16:17.450 --> 16:19.290
Like hell we'd lose!

16:19.720 --> 16:24.290
<i>After Nankatsu's goal, the match resumes with Hanawa's kick-off.</i>

16:24.290 --> 16:26.210
Let's do this, Masao!

16:26.210 --> 16:27.040
Yes.

16:30.170 --> 16:33.920
<i>The trump card of Hanawa's offense, the Tachibana Twins...</i>

16:33.920 --> 16:39.020
<i>Just as planned, their attacks are stopped by Nankatsu's aces, Tsubasa and Misaki.</i>

16:39.020 --> 16:41.600
<i>The plan works without a hitch!</i>

16:41.600 --> 16:47.430
<i>Right after conceding a goal to Nankatsu at the very beginning of the first half and letting Tsubasa take a single shot,</i>

16:47.430 --> 16:51.160
<i>Hanawa defends with all their might against Nankatsu's fierce attacks.</i>

16:51.160 --> 16:53.100
<i>And, even though Nankatsu continued to attack,</i>

16:53.100 --> 16:55.070
<i>they didn't concede another goal.</i>

16:55.070 --> 16:57.860
Nankatsu! It's time to score another one!

16:57.860 --> 17:00.910
What a drag! Their defense is so solid.

17:00.910 --> 17:02.700
Keep your defenses up, Hanawa!

17:02.700 --> 17:06.120
<i>It looks like Nankatsu has the advantage after all.</i>

17:06.120 --> 17:09.790
<i>On Hanawa's side, the Tachibana Twins are completely held down.</i>

17:11.550 --> 17:14.670
<i>The referee's whistle marks the end of the first half!</i>

17:14.670 --> 17:18.290
<i>In this last match of the group stage, Nankatsu vs. Hanawa,</i>

17:18.290 --> 17:20.190
<i>the first half ends, 1-0!</i>

17:20.190 --> 17:22.600
<i>Nankatsu holds a one goal lead over Hanawa!</i>

17:26.020 --> 17:27.810
You did well, boys.

17:27.810 --> 17:33.080
It'd be great to have another goal, but we still stuck to our plan

17:33.080 --> 17:34.490
and stopped the attacks of the Tachibana Twins.

17:34.490 --> 17:35.440
Yes!

17:35.440 --> 17:37.930
All right! Let's widen the lead in the second half,

17:37.930 --> 17:40.280
blow our opponents away and emerge victorious from the group stage!

17:40.280 --> 17:41.580
Yeah!

17:42.160 --> 17:45.450
Let's keep marking the Tachibana Twins in the second half, too.

17:45.450 --> 17:46.290
Yes.

17:46.760 --> 17:49.210
Nankatsu is dictating the flow of the match.

17:49.210 --> 17:53.550
If they keep this up, there's no doubt they will win.

17:54.510 --> 17:57.340
What should we do, Kazuo, Masao?

17:57.340 --> 18:00.140
Should we join in the attack too?

18:02.670 --> 18:05.680
Don't you trust us?

18:05.680 --> 18:08.350
But we won't be able to score at this rate.

18:08.350 --> 18:11.960
Don't worry. We still have an ace up our sleeves.

18:11.960 --> 18:13.280
What? An ace?

18:13.280 --> 18:14.070
Yes.

18:14.070 --> 18:17.310
I really didn't want to show it during the group stage,

18:17.310 --> 18:18.910
but it looks like there's no other way around it, Kazuo.

18:18.910 --> 18:20.820
Yes.

18:20.820 --> 18:23.870
<i>If we use that, we can quickly turn things around.</i>

18:24.420 --> 18:27.300
I honestly had a lot of hope in Hanawa.

18:27.300 --> 18:29.080
Well, they proved to be worthless in the end.

18:29.080 --> 18:30.030
Eh?

18:30.030 --> 18:32.750
I made sure we tied against Hanawa on purpose.

18:32.750 --> 18:33.840
What!?

18:33.840 --> 18:37.760
The only threat to us winning the championship is Nankatsu.

18:37.760 --> 18:40.760
I understood that clearly during our first match.

18:40.760 --> 18:45.010
So I tried to get rid of them before the group stage was over.

18:45.010 --> 18:47.560
To do that, I purposefully made sure we tied our game with Hanawa.

18:47.560 --> 18:50.590
I created a scenario where, even if Hanawa ties with Nankatsu in this game,

18:50.590 --> 18:55.440
Hanawa can still advance to the finals.

18:55.440 --> 18:57.540
But it looks like that won't work.

18:57.540 --> 18:59.610
Nankatsu is coming through, right?

18:59.610 --> 19:05.280
Yes. And there's something else that bothers me about Nankatsu.

19:07.540 --> 19:09.700
Genzo, that is...?

19:09.700 --> 19:13.850
I need to make sure I stay in shape for the finals.

19:13.850 --> 19:14.620
What?!

19:14.620 --> 19:16.280
I'll go even if you stop me.

19:16.280 --> 19:18.280
Nankatsu will beat Hanawa,

19:18.280 --> 19:23.590
and I'll return to protect Nankatsu in the grand finals!

19:24.800 --> 19:26.310
<i>The second half starts!</i>

19:26.310 --> 19:29.730
<i>Will Nankatsu be able to maintain their rhythm?</i>

19:29.730 --> 19:34.150
<i>Will Hanawa be able recover from the thorough marking of the Tachibana Twins in the first half?</i>

19:34.150 --> 19:35.820
We'll score a second goal—this time, for sure!

19:35.820 --> 19:38.110
<i>It seems Hanawa hasn't wavered yet, and are fiercely fighting back!</i>

19:38.110 --> 19:40.780
Attack, Hanawa! Attack, Hanawa!

19:42.380 --> 19:42.990
Masao!

19:43.550 --> 19:44.280
Nice!

19:44.280 --> 19:45.740
Got it! Run for it, Kazuo!

19:45.740 --> 19:46.720
Yes!

19:46.720 --> 19:49.220
<i>What's this?!</i>

19:49.220 --> 19:51.190
<i>The Tachibana Twins, who have always remained close</i>

19:51.190 --> 19:53.290
<i>and pushed through the middle field together are far apart from each other this time!</i>

19:53.290 --> 19:55.540
There's something at hand, here!

19:55.540 --> 19:57.500
Can you really afford to something like that? Here!

19:59.710 --> 20:00.970
You're about to eat your words!

20:00.970 --> 20:02.680
Something is definitely going on here.

20:03.120 --> 20:05.430
Masao, he's coming again!

20:05.430 --> 20:07.100
I hear you!

20:07.100 --> 20:08.850
Okay, I'm good to go, Masao!

20:08.850 --> 20:10.020
Okay!

20:12.850 --> 20:15.430
<i>Masao kicks the ball forward as hard as he can!</i>

20:15.430 --> 20:16.650
I couldn't make it...!

20:16.650 --> 20:18.650
<i>The ball is flying in front of the goal.</i>

20:18.650 --> 20:26.110
<i>Kazuo is there, but Takasugi is nearby and Nishio and Tsubasa are strictly marking him!</i>

20:27.660 --> 20:31.400
<i>Kazuo starts running... away from the ball!</i>

20:31.400 --> 20:31.910
<i>What!?</i>

20:34.380 --> 20:35.670
Here goes!

20:36.420 --> 20:40.460
<i>What was that?! He used the goalpost to jump!</i>

20:40.460 --> 20:41.090
What?

20:42.590 --> 20:43.220
Good!

20:43.220 --> 20:44.800
Come, Kazuo!

20:44.800 --> 20:47.420
<i>Masao is dashing forward!</i>

20:49.950 --> 20:51.140
<i>He shoots!</i>

20:51.660 --> 20:53.020
<i>Goal!</i>

20:53.520 --> 20:56.120
<i>Hanawa ties the game!</i>

20:56.120 --> 20:59.900
Did you see our Triangle Shot?

20:59.900 --> 21:00.900
Watch out!

21:00.900 --> 21:02.280
Move!

21:02.280 --> 21:04.280
CRASHHHHHH

21:06.530 --> 21:13.200
<i>Oh, no! Kazuo Tachibana who had jumped high into the air, and Nankatsu's Nishio who had tried to make the block</i>

21:13.200 --> 21:14.830
<i>crash hard into each other!</i>

21:14.830 --> 21:16.380
Hey, are you all right?

21:16.380 --> 21:16.990
Yeah.

21:16.990 --> 21:18.330
Nishio!

21:19.460 --> 21:20.320
Nishio!

21:20.320 --> 21:21.840
Hey, you're bleeding!

21:21.840 --> 21:24.670
This isn't good...

21:25.670 --> 21:29.590
<i>It looks like Nishio won't be able to keep playing.</i>

21:29.590 --> 21:30.930
<i>He's being carried away.</i>

21:32.260 --> 21:33.320
Nishio!

21:33.320 --> 21:34.640
I'm fine...!

21:34.640 --> 21:37.250
At such an important time...This is so lame.

21:38.730 --> 21:42.020
Ishizaki, you'll be replacing Nishio.

21:42.020 --> 21:43.820
What? Me!?

21:44.860 --> 21:48.570
All right! Then it's my turn to shine.

21:49.180 --> 21:52.900
<i>Player change for Nankatsu.</i>

21:52.900 --> 21:59.960
<i>#14 Ishizaki replaces #3 Nishio.</i>

21:59.960 --> 22:02.170
Let's do this!

22:02.170 --> 22:03.950
- Ishizaki! - Ishizaki!

22:03.950 --> 22:05.370
We're counting on you, Ishizaki!

22:05.370 --> 22:07.170
All right, leave it to me!

22:07.170 --> 22:09.090
Ishizaki's on the field!

22:09.090 --> 22:11.800
Do your best, Ishizaki!

22:11.800 --> 22:14.060
I might be lacking in technique compared to everyone,

22:14.060 --> 22:18.160
but I won't lose when it comes to guts!

22:20.060 --> 23:50.070
GENERIC TSUBASA ED. BRING IN THE MISUGI ED ALREADY

22:38.790 --> 22:44.670
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:44.670
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.670 --> 22:50.680
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.670 --> 22:50.680
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.680 --> 22:56.690
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.680 --> 22:56.690
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.690 --> 23:02.150
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.690 --> 23:02.150
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.110 --> 23:08.280
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.110 --> 23:08.280
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.200 --> 23:15.000
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.200 --> 23:15.000
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.000 --> 23:21.040
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.040 --> 23:26.050
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.040 --> 23:26.050
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.340 --> 23:33.220
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.340 --> 23:33.220
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.220 --> 23:39.100
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.100 --> 23:45.990
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.100 --> 23:45.990
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.070 --> 24:00.640
COMING SOON, EPISODE 17:
4 MINUTES LEFT! A DECISIVE BATTLE IN MID-AIR!
